WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.790
VICTOR DAVIS HANSON:
Right now, many Americans

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:06.112
have to be vaccinated
against the COVID virus,

00:00:06.112 --> 00:00:08.070
or they're not allowed
to teach, or they're not

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:09.420
allowed to work in a hospital.

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:12.730
Yet the two million people that
are coming across the border,

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:15.090
there's no requirement
that they be tested,

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:17.640
or there's no requirement
that they be vaccinated.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.190
So the United States, of
all countries in the world,

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:25.260
at its very founding
had the idea

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.960
that you could
become an American

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:32.220
if you crossed the borders and
you accepted the American idea.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:36.690
So when people came from diverse
countries, they had skills,

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:39.780
they spoke English,
and they came legally,

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:43.740
and there was not whole
blocs of ethnic castes

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:48.450
that had grievances or they had
difficulties in assimilation

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:50.130
with the majority population.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:52.200
And more importantly,
legal immigration

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:56.190
was welcomed because it
kind of reminded Americans

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:59.310
that there were people
who were very competitive,

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:02.700
and they wanted this system
of free market economics,

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.860
constitutional government,
a bill of rights

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.900
that was lacking in
their home country.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:10.590
What happens when the host
itself, i.e., the United

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:14.040
States, has lost confidence
in its traditions and customs

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.790
and doesn't feel that
it should or has a right

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:21.690
or it wouldn't be nice to impose
their values on people who

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:23.490
are arriving across a border?

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:26.250
Then, immigration
turns from something

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:29.730
very desirable and positive
to something that can be

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:31.440
very pernicious and dangerous.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:33.180
The corporate
establishment has been

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:36.420
a big advocate of open borders.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:39.210
And it's been very hard to
write op-eds for the Wall Street

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:41.310
Journal or talk to the
Chamber of Commerce

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:44.040
because they feel
that immigration,

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:48.720
even if it's illegal, is very
good for their own bottom line.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:52.620
And the Democratic Party
said, if you come illegally,

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:55.170
we will ensure that
you will not be

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:57.960
subject to the enforcement
of immigration laws.

00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:59.850
We will provide you
with entitlements,

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:04.530
but we expect, in exchange,
fealty and loyalty and fidelity

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:05.430
at the polls.

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:10.560
And it explains why now we do
not enforce immigration law,

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.410
because too many parties have
too many vested interests.

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:14.880
And we look at the border.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:16.680
And it is a construct.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:18.660
It doesn't exist in reality.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:20.820
People are simply
walking across.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:23.280
And you have people
coming in vast numbers

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:24.870
from one direction.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:26.670
They do not speak English.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:27.780
They're not legal.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.790
And we, the host,
are not the host

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:32.850
that we have been from
the prior 280 years.

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:36.150
But we feel diffident,
lack of confidence

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:37.590
about our own system.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:41.250
We don't feel we want to
impose on our new visitors.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:43.560
We feel it would be
cultural appropriation

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:46.350
to tell them that this
system is better than the one

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:47.100
they're leaving.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:51.480
You add all of that up, and
you have chaos and the erosion

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:52.680
of the idea of citizenship.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:56.030
[MUSIC PLAYING]

